Rock, paper, scissors!

266
00:09:26,033 --> 00:09:27,433
Rock, paper, scissors!

267
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,167
(Bottoms +1 point) Yeah!

268
00:09:29,167 --> 00:09:30,333
Finally!

269
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:33,733
(Maybe we should let them go first) Maybe a good top should let the bottom win.

270
00:09:33,733 --> 00:09:34,733
Fine with me.

271
00:09:34,733 --> 00:09:36,467
This is a game. Doesn't count!

272
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,133
The tops will try to score.

273
00:09:39,133 --> 00:09:42,600
The bottoms have to defend and keep the balls off the boards.

274
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,267
You guys have two minutes.

275
00:09:44,267 --> 00:09:46,467
Judging by their stance, victory looks unlikely.

276
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:47,967
(You're up for it, right?) Very scary.

277
00:09:47,967 --> 00:09:49,800
Okay, if you're ready...

278
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:50,733
Go!

279
00:09:50,833 --> 00:09:51,900
Take it easy.

280
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:55,933
(Lena means business.)

281
00:09:55,933 --> 00:09:58,467
I'm... I'm... I'm scared. I'm so scared.

282
00:10:04,067 --> 00:10:05,700
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

283
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:07,100
Lena!

284
00:10:07,133 --> 00:10:08,067
That's cheating!

285
00:10:09,733 --> 00:10:10,733
Oi!

286
00:10:20,767 --> 00:10:22,267
Two, one!

287
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,600
(Time's up!) Time's up!

288
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:26,833
- I'm dying! - I'm dying!

289
00:10:26,867 --> 00:10:28,000
Oh, that was a lot!

290
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,867
(Tops scored 18 points.) I'm exhausted. / 18 points!

291
00:10:32,067 --> 00:10:33,133
Lena...

292
00:10:33,933 --> 00:10:35,600
You're good at shooting hoops.

293
00:10:36,633 --> 00:10:37,867
Since when?

294
00:10:39,233 --> 00:10:40,467
(That took a lot of energy) I surrender.

295
00:10:40,467 --> 00:10:42,300
That took as much energy as *.

296
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:44,633
Before we start, anything you wanna say to the bottoms?

297
00:10:44,633 --> 00:10:45,733
Nope. Let's start.

298
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:47,567
(Ready?) Okay.

299
00:10:47,767 --> 00:10:48,567
Ready?

300
00:10:48,567 --> 00:10:50,700
If you're ready, Bam...

301
00:10:50,700 --> 00:10:51,733
Press it!

302
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:53,100
Go ahead and press it!

303
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:56,167
Three, two, one!

304
00:11:05,033 --> 00:11:07,033
(Everyone's going all out!)

305
00:11:12,367 --> 00:11:16,867
Four, three, two, one!

306
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:18,900
Whoo!

307
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,200
I'm dying!

308
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:23,500
(Everyone's completely worn out.) I stopped jumping when I saw they won.

309
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,433
- I'm exhausted. - I can't.

310
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:26,967
(Bottoms scored 25 points.) Bam's the MVP.

311
00:11:26,967 --> 00:11:29,167
- Whoa! Whoa! Whoa! - Hurry!

312
00:11:30,667 --> 00:11:31,800
(The caretaker rushed over.)

313
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,600
Yu just kept throwing.

314
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,100
(Quantity over quality) But I didn't hit once.

315
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:37,300
- Bam has so much energy. - For real.

316
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:38,967
I didn't notice anyone. I wasn't focused on them.

317
00:11:38,967 --> 00:11:40,667
- I was only focused on the target. - The goal.

318
00:11:40,667 --> 00:11:43,467
"Goals are there to be tackled," said Bam Saralee.

319
00:11:43,867 --> 00:11:46,900
I didn't think HarborLand would be like this.

320
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:48,167
(Miu stands by what she said)

321
00:11:48,167 --> 00:11:49,300
She proudly presented it.

322
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,900
"Everyone, we're going on an adventure!"

323
00:11:51,900 --> 00:11:54,233
"We'll do things like..." What was it? Zip-lining.

324
00:11:54,233 --> 00:11:55,333
And then she said,

325
00:11:55,333 --> 00:11:57,433
"You have to play every game with me!"

326
00:11:57,433 --> 00:11:58,500
Yeah.

327
00:11:58,833 --> 00:11:59,900
How's that working out?

328
00:11:59,933 --> 00:12:01,267
How's that working out?

329
00:12:01,967 --> 00:12:04,433
Gotta do research next time. Don't make stuff up.

330
00:12:04,633 --> 00:12:06,800
Hello there!

331
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,800
We've just finished Mission 2.

332
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:10,200
We're heading to Mission 3.

333
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:13,000
I went out of my way to wear kids' clothes.

334
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,200
But this isn't what I expected at all.

335
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:18,133
I was looking forward to slides, hanging out, zip-lining.

336
00:12:18,133 --> 00:12:19,800
I expected none of this!

337
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:20,700
It's so hot.

338
00:12:20,700 --> 00:12:23,600
At first, it was cold in the last room, right?

339
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,867
Because the AC was blowing right on me. But it's hot in here.

340
00:12:26,867 --> 00:12:27,867
I can't take it.

341
00:12:27,867 --> 00:12:29,467
The way you stretch...

342
00:12:29,467 --> 00:12:30,867
Can I go through here?

343
00:12:32,500 --> 00:12:34,600
Look at this. It's too revealing.

344
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,900
Is it too revealing?

345
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:38,033
Right? Is it too revealing?

346
00:12:38,033 --> 00:12:39,867
- It's... - It's fine. It's hot.

347
00:12:39,867 --> 00:12:40,933
Is it too revealing?

348
00:12:43,167 --> 00:12:44,200
Trust me.

349
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,433
I've got my eye on you.

350
00:12:45,433 --> 00:12:46,433
Just like that.

351
00:12:46,433 --> 00:12:47,233
How?

352
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,367
(Game 3: The Balance Battle) The Balance Battle:

353
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,233
a balancing competition on a beam.

354
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:57,500
Each team must throw their opponents off balance

355
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:59,267
and make them fall down.

356
00:12:59,267 --> 00:13:02,100
The team with the most points wins.

357
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,867
You will compete one pair at a time.

358
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:05,867
Let's welcome...

359
00:13:05,867 --> 00:13:08,367
(Match 1: Oom vs. Bam) Oom and Bam!

360
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:10,767
Go, Eisaya! Go, Eisaya!

361
00:13:10,767 --> 00:13:12,833
- Saralee, get her! - Come on, Eisaya!

362
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:16,267
Bam! Saralam! Saralam! Saralam! Whoo!

363
00:13:16,267 --> 00:13:19,167
Eisaya, come on! Eisaya!

364
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:21,033
Bam, do you have anything to say to Oom?

365
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:22,933
(Which side do you prefer?) Wanna fall left or right?

366
00:13:24,933 --> 00:13:26,467
(I wanna fall into your heart.) I wanna fall into your heart.

367
00:13:26,467 --> 00:13:28,000
(I wanna fall into your heart.) I wanna fall into your heart.

368
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:31,333
Don't!

369
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:33,100
You flirt too! Don't stop her!

370
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:35,933
Already losing my balance.

371
00:13:36,567 --> 00:13:38,400
If you're ready...

372
00:13:38,633 --> 00:13:39,300
Go!

373
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,600
Bam, you got this!

374
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,667
Watch out, Bam.

375
00:13:41,667 --> 00:13:42,633
Don't...

376
00:13:42,633 --> 00:13:43,433
Yeah!

377
00:13:43,433 --> 00:13:45,100
Make eye contact and seduce her.

378
00:13:45,133 --> 00:13:46,067
Yes!

379
00:13:46,067 --> 00:13:48,400
Mesmerize her! Whoa, Bam!

380
00:13:50,967 --> 00:13:51,900
(Over in a flash)

381
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:52,933
Huh?

382
00:13:52,933 --> 00:13:56,400
Get back up! One more round! I didn't even do anything.

383
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,367
One more round? Sure.

384
00:13:57,367 --> 00:13:58,333
One more round.

385
00:13:58,333 --> 00:13:59,200
Oom says no.

386
00:13:59,233 --> 00:14:01,833
(She gets a rematch) Oom says that was just practice.

387
00:14:01,833 --> 00:14:04,100
- Okay, if you're ready, go! - This is scary!

388
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,100
Go, go, go!

389
00:14:05,933 --> 00:14:07,533
You got this. You got this.

390
00:14:07,633 --> 00:14:08,167
Go.

391
00:14:09,867 --> 00:14:11,900
Oom's too scared. Ah, there you go!

392
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:12,733
Yeah, yeah!

393
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,333
They're like two ants fighting.

394
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:20,833
(Bam Saralee wins.)

395
00:14:20,833 --> 00:14:22,267
Oom, she's hurt!

396
00:14:22,533 --> 00:14:23,500
Really? Are you hurt?

397
00:14:23,500 --> 00:14:24,367
Her head. Just now.

398
00:14:24,400 --> 00:14:25,467
Aww!

399
00:14:25,833 --> 00:14:27,467
Really? Did I hit your head?

400
00:14:27,467 --> 00:14:28,233
What's wrong?

401
00:14:28,467 --> 00:14:29,267
Where?

402
00:14:29,267 --> 00:14:31,200
Check on her. Check on her, Oom.

403
00:14:33,367 --> 00:14:35,233
(Almost fell for it.) Just like Lalynn.

404
00:14:35,667 --> 00:14:38,167
- Faking just like Lalynn. - I need another acting lesson.

405
00:14:39,567 --> 00:14:40,467
I'm going home.

406
00:14:40,467 --> 00:14:41,533
TanYu!

407
00:14:41,533 --> 00:14:43,833
(Match 2: Tan vs. YuYu) That's right! / Really?

408
00:14:43,833 --> 00:14:44,700
Jeez.

409
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:47,667
Tan, do you have anything to say to Yu?

410
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:50,100
Yu said she likes to stumble.

411
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,433
You can stumble into me.

412
00:14:51,433 --> 00:14:53,400
(You can stumble into me.)

413
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,633
- I'll stumble over, then knock her off. - Excuse me.

414
00:14:55,633 --> 00:14:56,667
What?

415
00:14:56,667 --> 00:14:57,667
Excuse me.

416
00:14:57,667 --> 00:14:58,567
In my heart.

417
00:14:58,567 --> 00:14:59,667
Yes, Miu?

418
00:15:00,067 --> 00:15:02,400
(Why are you flirting here?) Why are you flirting here? I don't get it.

419
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:03,967
I seriously don't get it.

420
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,300
Flirt with her. I'll wait.

421
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,000
No need. I won her over ages ago.

422
00:15:10,667 --> 00:15:11,400
Okay.

423
00:15:11,400 --> 00:15:12,467
(Too shy to handle it.)

424
00:15:12,467 --> 00:15:14,300
If you're ready...

425
00:15:14,300 --> 00:15:15,200
Go!

426
00:15:15,267 --> 00:15:17,867
- Go! Yu, you got this. - But Yu's really strong.

427
00:15:17,867 --> 00:15:21,467
Yu, fight to the end! Yu, show them what you've got! Yu, you got this!

428
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:30,233
(Tan wins.)

429
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,767
Hey! Hey!

430
00:15:37,267 --> 00:15:39,400
(Match 3: Lena vs. Miu) The other pairs were like ants fighting.

431
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,867
(So you're gonna clobber me?) So you're gonna clobber me?

432
00:15:40,867 --> 00:15:41,867
Let's wait and see.

433
00:15:41,867 --> 00:15:42,667
Okay.

434
00:15:42,667 --> 00:15:44,733
- You got this! Miu, you got this! - If you're ready...

435
00:15:44,733 --> 00:15:45,567
Go!

436
00:15:45,567 --> 00:15:46,867
Come on, Miu!

437
00:15:47,333 --> 00:15:48,900
Hey, hold it like this.

438
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:50,000
(Already fighting) Says who?

439
00:15:50,433 --> 00:15:52,133
(You're gonna get it!) Fine!

440
00:15:55,467 --> 00:15:58,233
- Miu, don't do that! - Yeah, don't do that.

441
00:16:06,567 --> 00:16:09,133
And the winner is Miu!

442
00:16:09,133 --> 00:16:10,500
(Miu wins.)

443
00:16:12,667 --> 00:16:14,200
I can't do this anymore.

444
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,367
She came at me...

445
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,033
This spot's sinking.

446
00:16:18,033 --> 00:16:19,400
Yeah, yeah.

447
00:16:19,833 --> 00:16:23,333
That game ended quickly. I barely had to use any strength.

448
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:25,267
(A clear-cut win) A great little break

449
00:16:25,267 --> 00:16:28,867
before we move on to the big stage, the real deal, the next game.

450
00:16:28,867 --> 00:16:30,667
Bam and Miu were awesome.

451
00:16:30,933 --> 00:16:33,033
They're the village's last hope!

452
00:16:33,900 --> 00:16:35,500
(We got it.) We got it, right?

453
00:16:35,500 --> 00:16:36,433
Yes.

454
00:16:36,667 --> 00:16:39,533
Yep, totally. She meant she got to fall.

455
00:16:39,733 --> 00:16:42,500
I'm not great at balancing. I'm a bit tilted.

456
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,500
(Can I stumble over to you?) The world's tilted, right? / True.

457
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,933
Yu likes to stumble.

458
00:16:46,767 --> 00:16:47,833
Ninja Game.

459
00:16:47,833 --> 00:16:50,500
Each team must search for treasure targets

460
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,233
spread across six floors.

461
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:53,900
They have 10 minutes.

462
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:56,567
The team with the most points wins.

463
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:59,033
(The bottoms go first) Our mission is to find the treasure.

464
00:16:59,033 --> 00:17:01,867
Whenever we find one of these stations, we have to tap it

465
00:17:01,867 --> 00:17:03,933
to collect points on each floor.

466
00:17:03,933 --> 00:17:06,599
So we'll split up by floor.

467
00:17:06,599 --> 00:17:08,032
I'll take the upper floors.

468
00:17:08,032 --> 00:17:09,532
Miu takes 5th and 6th floors.

469
00:17:09,532 --> 00:17:11,400
3rd and 4th. I take 1st and 2nd.

470
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,166
There are 80 targets to collect

471
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:14,767
(80 targets!) in 10 minutes. / 80?!

472
00:17:15,032 --> 00:17:16,000
80 targets.

473
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,599
(80 targets / 3 people) 80 divided by 3.

474
00:17:18,967 --> 00:17:20,300
(Miu's in shock)

475
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:22,567
- We don't have to get them all. - Just collect more than they do.

476
00:17:22,567 --> 00:17:23,567
- Okay. - We got this!

477
00:17:23,567 --> 00:17:24,367
We got this!

478
00:17:24,367 --> 00:17:26,067
If you're ready...

479
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:27,333
Go!

480
00:17:31,200 --> 00:17:33,733
I have to go up to the next floor. Hup! Hup!

481
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:41,000
Guys, there are so few of them.

482
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,733
We don't need 10 minutes. We...

483
00:17:42,733 --> 00:17:43,833
It's spinning.

484
00:17:48,533 --> 00:17:49,567
Can I tap it now?

485
00:17:49,567 --> 00:17:50,500
Yea, just tap it.

486
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:51,500
Oh, no need to wait.

487
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:52,833
No, no need. Go, go.

488
00:17:54,567 --> 00:17:55,633
Does blue mean no?

489
00:17:56,933 --> 00:17:57,967
Can you find any?

490
00:18:01,433 --> 00:18:03,267
- There are actually quite a lot. - Yeah.

491
00:18:03,267 --> 00:18:04,400
I've already tapped that.

492
00:18:04,433 --> 00:18:06,467
Yeah. Should we go up or not?

493
00:18:06,467 --> 00:18:08,067
The upper floors are Miu's.

494
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:09,300
- This one... - Okay.

495
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:12,667
Whoa, how do I get in there?

496
00:18:12,667 --> 00:18:13,933
- Whoa! - You have to crawl.

497
00:18:13,933 --> 00:18:14,733
Whoa!

498
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,467
(Going all out)

499
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:19,167
Whoa!

500
00:18:25,633 --> 00:18:28,400
Oh, this floor is so dark. Oh no, I'm scared.

501
00:18:28,733 --> 00:18:31,200
- Don't ditch me. I'm afraid of the dark. - You got it.

502
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:44,233
I've already got this one, right?

503
00:18:44,233 --> 00:18:45,033
Tap!

504
00:18:45,567 --> 00:18:46,400
Yeah.

505
00:18:59,233 --> 00:19:00,333
Are there any left?

506
00:19:01,633 --> 00:19:02,533
Okay.

507
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:05,200
Let's go down. Find a way down. There's a slide here.

508
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,100
Are we done?

509
00:19:06,133 --> 00:19:08,000
Great job! Yay!

510
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:09,433
- Are you done? - I am.

511
00:19:09,433 --> 00:19:11,300
- We're done. Let's go. - We're done.

512
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:13,300
Bam, are there any left down there?

513
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,267
Nope, all done!

514
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:16,233
Are we being timed, too?

515
00:19:16,233 --> 00:19:17,600
(They did great on time.)

516
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:18,700
Miu, hurry up!

517
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:20,333
Guys, we're done!

518
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:22,267
Best score.

519
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:24,800
Oh, second place today!

520
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:26,700
- Really? - Second place today!

521
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,200
Oh, Miu got first place!

522
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,233
(Today's top score)

523
00:19:29,233 --> 00:19:31,133
Bam's second, and I'm third today.

524
00:19:31,133 --> 00:19:32,467
Great job!

525
00:19:33,033 --> 00:19:34,100
Great job!

526
00:19:34,333 --> 00:19:35,300
(Bottoms: 26,000 points) We got 26,000.

527
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,467
(Bottoms: 26,000 points) Let's see how many points the tops will get.

528
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,533
What was the other team's name?

529
00:19:40,533 --> 00:19:41,200
- Uke. - Huh?

530
00:19:41,233 --> 00:19:43,300
LOT! Short for Lena, Oom, and Tan.

531
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:46,033
(Time for the tops) How about Lotte? It's a word. Or just LOT?

532
00:19:46,033 --> 00:19:46,833
LOT works for me.

533
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:48,833
